==> .github/DEPLOY.md <==
# Deploying demo

The **Deploy** workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) builds every image,
pushes it to `ghcr.io/example`, writes the
application's environment to `.env`, and runs `./deploy.sh`. Start it
from the repository's **Actions** tab → **Deploy** → **Run workflow**.

## Repository secrets

Add these under **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions**.

### Image registry

- `GHCR_TOKEN` — a token that can push and pull images on
  `ghcr.io` as `example`.

### Deploy

<!-- --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) --- -->
- `DEPLOY_HOST` — Hostname or IP of the swarm manager.
<!-- --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) --- -->
- `DEPLOY_USER` — SSH user on DEPLOY_HOST that can run docker. Optional; defaults to root.
<!-- --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) --- -->
- `DEPLOY_SSH_KEY` — Private SSH key for DEPLOY_USER.
<!-- --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) --- -->
- `DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS` — DEPLOY_HOST's known_hosts line(s), from `ssh-keyscan DEPLOY_HOST`. Optional, but without it the host key is trusted on first use.

### Application environment

Written to `.env` on every deploy.

<!-- --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) --- -->
- `DATABASE_URL` — Postgres connection string
<!-- --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) --- -->
- `JWT_SECRET` — Secret used to sign auth tokens
<!-- --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) --- -->
- `CORS_ORIGINS` — Comma-separated allowed CORS origins

==> .github/workflows/deploy.yml <==
name: Deploy

on:
  workflow_dispatch:

# Never cancel a deploy halfway through; queue the next one instead.
concurrency:
  group: deploy
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3

      - uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          registry: ghcr.io
          username: example
          password: ${{ secrets.GHCR_TOKEN }}

      # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (oci-image@1) ---
      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v5
        with:
          context: ./demo-api
          file: ./demo-api/Dockerfile
          push: true
          tags: |
            ghcr.io/example/demo-api:${{ github.sha }}
            ghcr.io/example/demo-api:latest
          cache-from: type=gha,scope=demo-api
          cache-to: type=gha,mode=max,scope=demo-api

  deploy:
    needs: build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          registry: ghcr.io
          username: example
          password: ${{ secrets.GHCR_TOKEN }}

      # Secrets arrive as environment variables, never pasted into the
      # script, so their values can't break or inject into it.
      - name: Write .env
        env:
          ENV_FILE: .env
          # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
          DATABASE_URL: ${{ secrets.DATABASE_URL }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
          JWT_SECRET: ${{ secrets.JWT_SECRET }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
          CORS_ORIGINS: ${{ secrets.CORS_ORIGINS }}
        run: |
          {
            : # valid even when nothing provides env@1
            # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
            printf '%s=%s\n' DATABASE_URL "$DATABASE_URL"
            # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
            printf '%s=%s\n' JWT_SECRET "$JWT_SECRET"
            # --- ci/github-actions for backend/go-grpc-gateway (env@1) ---
            printf '%s=%s\n' CORS_ORIGINS "$CORS_ORIGINS"
          } >"$ENV_FILE"

      - name: Deploy
        env:
          IMAGE_TAG: ${{ github.sha }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) ---
          DEPLOY_HOST: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_HOST }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) ---
          DEPLOY_USER: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_USER }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) ---
          DEPLOY_SSH_KEY: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_SSH_KEY }}
          # --- ci/github-actions for runtime/docker-swarm (deploy-secret@1) ---
          DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS }}
        run: ./deploy.sh

==> Caddyfile <==
{
	email admin@example.com
	# Caddy stores certs in the caddy_data volume — persisted across restarts.
	# No init script, no reload hooks, no certbot. It just works.
}

demo.example.com {
	# --- edge/caddy for backend/go-grpc-gateway (http-service@2) ---
	handle /* {
		reverse_proxy demo-api:8080 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
		}
	}
}

